-------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. WHAT YOU MAY DO, WITHOUT ASKING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

You may:

  a) Read the source code.

  b) Build it and run it. On as many computers as you like, at home or at
     work, for money or not.

  c) Change your own copy, and run your changed copy yourself or inside your
     own company.

  d) Copy the software to give to someone else, UNCHANGED, and only if you
     keep this licence file with it and say where it came from.

  e) Quote small pieces of the code in a review, article, tutorial or
     teaching material, as long as you say it is from Snatch and name the
     author.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. WHAT YOU MUST ASK PERMISSION FOR
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

You must get written permission from Ayoub Zulfiqar BEFORE you:

  a) Publish a fork. That means putting your changed copy anywhere other
     people can get it, under any name.

  b) Share a changed copy with anyone outside your own household or company.

  c) Sell the software, or sell anything that includes it.

  d) Put it in an app store, package repository, or any other place people
     download software from.

  e) Take a meaningful part of the code and use it in another project.

"Written permission" means an email from ayoubzulfiqar3@gmail.com saying yes.
Permission is often given. Asking costs you one email.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. CREDIT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Wherever you are allowed to share this, or you get permission to, you must
credit the author clearly and where people will see it:

    Based on Snatch by Ayoub Zulfiqar
    https://github.com/ayoubzulfiqar/snatch-dl

That credit must appear in at least one place a user will look: your README,
your about screen, your download page, or your app store listing.

You may not remove the author's name, the copyright notice, or this licence
from any copy.

You may not suggest that the author wrote, checked, or approved your version.


